 to let let the new  prime minister get on with his or her  job and make it clear that he's moved on  as well i do think that he hasn't done  that yet then i think he hasn't done it  yet okay thank you very much indeed uh  phillip halland  uh well a big program uh of course uh  today because it's gonna be a very big  week next week tomorrow we're gonna be  finding out  who will be uh the leader of the  conservative party uh tuesday is when of  course we will be finding out the prime  minister resigning and then on wednesday  will be another important day the first  meeting of the new uh cabinet the new  prime minister facing the commons for  the first time at prime minister's  questions and we can add to that list  the return of our midweek programme for  take as well uh so do uh come and join  us at 9pm on wednesdays it's our chance  to take the political temperature in the  middle of the week with some big  interviews a bit of analysis from the  journalists data on the state of play in  uk politics and a panel of viewers to  give us their take uh on all of the big  political news now if you want to be  involved in that conversation then do  please send us an email at the take with  safety ridge at sky dot uk the email  should be on your screens right now just  a couple of lines about yourself  and your politics and it's going to be a  pretty extraordinary week next week and  next wednesday as well so definitely  want to tune into there  well that is it for this week sophie  ridge on sunday it is good to be back in  a moment after the break we'll be  running through today's interviews  finding out what we learned with our  deputy political editor sam copes thanks  for joining us this sunday morning  [Music]  [Music]  we support communities to grow food in  lost and unloved spaces across the city  so our main kind of driving force is to  get people growing  [Music]

